Sketchreel voice model files

kokoro-v1.0.onnx (split into kokoro-v1.0.onnx.part01 … part07) and voices-v1.0.bin are the
Kokoro v1.0 ONNX model files published by thewh1teagle in the kokoro-onnx project
(https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx, release "model-files-v1.0"), unchanged.

Kokoro-82M, the model they come from, is by hexgrad (https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M)
and is released under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).
The kokoro-onnx project is released under the MIT License (see LICENSE-kokoro-onnx-MIT).

These copies are kept here, split into parts under GitHub's file size guideline, so that
Sketchreel's Claude voiceover can fetch them with git from github.com.

Pronunciation data for Sketchreel's own pronunciation engine

g2p-en.json.xz is the British English pronunciation lexicon of misaki by hexgrad
(https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki, data files gb_gold.json and gb_silver.json from the misaki 0.7.4 release),
merged into one file (gold entries over silver, default pronunciations only) and xz-compressed. misaki is released
under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

g2p-lts.json.xz is Sketchreel's English letter-to-sound table, learned from that lexicon by Sketchreel
(for names and words the lexicon doesn't have).

g2p-en-us.json.xz is misaki's American English lexicon (data files us_gold.json and us_silver.json from the same
misaki 0.7.4 release), merged and compressed the same way, and g2p-lts-us.json.xz is Sketchreel's letter-to-sound
table learned from it (Sketchreel's American voices, app v67).

